  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The café can show a return map on the counter and on small cards beside the cups.\", \"decision\": \"How should guests learn where to return cups?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nGuests look at the counter map before choosing a cup and take a return card if needed. The return route is considered before the loan begins.\nVolunteers give each guest a return card with the cup and point to the same route on the counter map. The return explanation accompanies the handover.\nVolunteers display the return cards beside the cups and use the counter map to answer questions afterward. Guests can learn the route themselves while help remains available."
    }
